{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/39963-departure-of-the-gods","id":39963,"title":"Departure of the Gods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-31T07:27:54-08:00","id":39963,"title":"Departure of the Gods","content":"As I understand the default Scion setting, the current generation of Scions is the first one in a long time, because the gods departed the World long ago and have only recently returned (i.e., roughly a generation back). There are alternate settings that set the gods\u2019 return further back (e.g., World at War) or posit that they\u2019ve been here all along; but these variants either have no impact on my question here or they render it moot:<br /> <br /> When did the gods depart the World, and why?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m assuming here for devout believers in a given mythology to continue to exist long after their Pantheon\u2019s departure, but that the gods always existed before, and overlapped with, their first worshippers. Indeed, I\u2019m assuming that one of the steps in establishing a Pantheon is founding a religion in the World that worships it; so while individual gods predate their earliest worshippers, Pantheons do not. Conversely, I don\u2019t think that any Pantheon that remained active in the World would have allowed their worship to be wiped out; so the departure of a given Pantheon should probably take place before (or, at the latest, during) the decline of their followers in the World . So with that in mind:<br /> <br /> Some Pantheons may have departed a long time ago indeed: the likes of the Pesedjet could have left the world many thousands of years ago. OTOH, the Loa as presented in 1e didn\u2019t even <i>exist</i> until three or four hundred years ago. If 2e goes with Orishas instead of Loa, or with Loa who are firmly rooted in African mythology rather than Caribbean syncretism, then they <i>could</i> have departed long before the slave trade started bringing their worshippers to the Americas; but even then, you have the likes of the Aesir and the Amatsukami, whose mythologies arose roughly one to two thousand years ago, and the Aztl\u00e1nti Pantheon was founded sometime in the thirteenth century AD. If you extend them back to include Toltec worshippers, you could have their founding be as far back as 650 AD; but that\u2019s <i>really</i> stretching things. With all that in mind, I\u2019d be inclined to set the last Pantheon\u2019s departure roughly five to six hundred years ago. That still gives the Aztl\u00e1nti a couple of centuries in the World. So <i>why</i> did the gods depart?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T07:42:51-08:00","id":39974,"title":"","content":"From what I understood, the reason the Gods departed was Fate. Fatebonds, to be exact. Now, I might be getting some of the details wrong because it's been ages since I read the corebook and I might be getting it mixed up with homebrew that's been headcanon for me for ages, but it all boils down to the fact that thanks to Fatebonds the Gods eventually found themselves getting shoehorned into roles or powers they didn't like, and decided to retreat from the World as a result. Also, I'm a fan of the idea that the Gods all made a pact and left together, partly because by your logic the Deva, Shen and Kami never left, and I do not like that idea. And as for why the older Pantheons let their worshipper base fall apart, perhaps it is because they felt the sting of Fatebonds first? So they simply decided it wasn't worth the added risk? And when the newer Pantheons felt the same thing happening to them, I can imagine the whole lot of them got together and took an executive decision to abandon the World. Only the threat of the Titans has brought them back. I wouldn't be surprised if, after the war is over, they leave once again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T11:34:37-08:00","id":40079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/39963-departure-of-the-gods?p=39974#post39974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm a fan of the idea that the Gods all made a pact and left together, partly because by your logic the Deva, Shen and Kami never left, and I do not like that idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is that \u201cby my logic\u201d? All my logic does is to pinpoint the <i>latest</i> point that a given Pantheon might have departed; they could have departed any time prior to that, up to, say, a century or two after their formation. All that my logic says about the Deva, Shen(?), and (Amatsu)kami is that there is no \u201clatest date\u201d cutoff imposed by the decline of their worship. In particular, I\u2019m <i>not</i> trying to establish any sort of causal link between the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T11:40:10-08:00","id":40082,"title":"","content":"I apologize. I misread the third paragraph of your post. That being said, what do you think of the Fatebond idea in general?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T12:10:23-08:00","id":40095,"title":"","content":"Well, Fatebinding <i>does</i> seem to be the primary mechanism for discouraging gods from running rampant in the World. But I\u2019m not sure it strikes me as enough of a reason for the gods to have left the World entirely, especially if they all did so at once; at the very least, I\u2019d expect there to be some sort of trigger event that brought things to a head. Frankly though, Fatebinding seems to be more of an \u201cinteract with the World in moderation\u201d thing rather than a \u201cstay away from the World at all costs\u201d thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T12:21:34-08:00","id":40102,"title":"","content":"Maybe Fate told them to? Perhaps all the Mystics and Prophets simultaneously received a 'Leave' message one fine morning? I know that sounds like a terrible reason, but Fate is explicitly the only force in Scion greater than Gods and Titans. I can't think of anything <i>else</i> that could simultaneously get every single Pantheon to leave their beloved playground behind. So, even if Fatebonds were not explicitly involved, I'd risk a wager that Fate had <i>something </i>to do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T13:45:04-08:00","id":40137,"title":"","content":"Well\u2026 it doesn\u2019t <i>have</i> to be simultaneous. But yes, Fate almost certainly should have been involved. Thing is, gods are notorious for rejecting Fate: it <s>rarely</s>never goes well for them when they do, but they nevertheless tend not to take orders well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T06:55:14-08:00","id":40491,"title":"","content":"The book says that they retreated, but it never says they were gone completely. The reasons for their retreat is suggested to be Fatebonds, but these retreats appear to be at different points in time after a pantheon has risen to power. Some pantheons have been in 'retreat' from the world hundreds of years before other pantheons were even formed. The reasons for this could be nearly infinite.<br /> <br /> On some level, I enjoy the idea that the world is incredibly boring to the gods. The people that inhabit it are weak, slow, fragile, droll, abrasive, ugly, blind, stupid, and sluggish (attribute respective). The divine realms would offer metaphysically infinite space to work and live within. They have surrounded themselves with things beautiful and entertaining beyond the ken of mortal comprehension. Their dramas and comedies are all 40+ successes. The beds they sleep upon are all 40+ successes. The food they eat is all 40+ successes. The very houses they live in are all 40+ successes. The most powerful of gods probably have all the above at the 100+ success range.<br /> <br /> The gods that choose to linger are the ones who are probably equivalent to mortals who choose to deal with animals. Some genuinely care for mortals like 'pets', some support 'animal' rights, some enjoy using 'animals' for sport, some study 'animals' and their habits, some probably don't care but might help an 'animal' in need if they saw one, some enjoy abusing the helpless, and some will fornicate with anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 01-01-2014, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T13:37:34-08:00","id":40700,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded again of the perspective I read in Wright's &quot;Titans of Chaos:&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You will not believe this now, but in times to come you may. The art and science, poetry and literature, philosophy and thought and myth of mankind exceed the best efforts of the immortal races. Our muses need their artists as much as their artists need our muses. What men had to teach was more rational, fair, and lofty, and in a word, <b>better</b>, than the lessons you would have learned from the Olympians. They are the creatures of Prometheus.<br /> How else was I to deal with a dangerous race of world-destroying monsters? If I taught them to reason, maybe they could be reasoned with.</i><br /> <br /> ---Boreus, explaining in part, of his reason to raise titanspawn as human children<br /> ----------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Of course in that book the gods were never gone. They're just worshipped differently.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Why do you hide from the humans?&quot;<br /> &quot;We need the worship. If they saw us as we were, they'd hate us.&quot;<br /> &quot;But they don't worship you, not the pagan gods, not anymore.&quot;<br /> &quot;My mom and dad are Lust and Violence. You telling me human beings don't worship them? We're in L.A.! Race riots and Hollywood. Men don't worship what they think they do, no matter what they say.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> ----A transformed Eros answering a few questions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":".  spelling 01-01-2014, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T11:39:07-08:00","id":60946,"title":"","content":"I remember reading somewhere that when the cultures started to meet and come into conflict, their Gods did also. Thor vs Zeus in the World is a bad day for everyone, and so to avoid the divine violence the Gods retreated to let their followers sort things out for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}